    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": 200,
      "gridPos": {"h": 8, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 28},
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### How to read this dashboard\n- **Patient-Impact Backlog tiles** answer: *who is being affected right now?* ADT backlog means bed managers and registration are working blind. Results backlog means clinicians are waiting on labs/imaging that already exist. Orders backlog means workups aren't reaching the lab/RIS/pharmacy. Claims backlog is revenue sitting still.\n- **Critical Interface Status table** sorts by queue depth. The top row is the workflow most at risk right now.\n- **Last Msg (s ago)** turns yellow at 5 min and red at 15 min — production ADT/Results interfaces should never go silent for that long during clinical hours.\n- **Clinical Message Throughput** is the line a CIO points at when asking \"why is our chart slow today?\" — a sustained dip in ADT or Results almost always traces back to upstream EHR/lab system trouble.\n\n### What this does NOT yet measure (next iterations)\n- True clinical SLAs (order → result turnaround, door → page time, discharge → PCP delivery) — needs message-level timestamps from HL7v2 MSH-7 vs delivery timestamp.\n- Patient counts behind a queue — needs per-message PID parsing to count *distinct patients* affected, not just *messages* queued.\n- Compliance metrics — Cures Act Patient Access API uptime, TEFCA QHIN delivery rate, info-blocking response time.\n- Cost-of-outage — wire revenue-per-claim and avg LOS impact-per-delayed-ADT to convert backlog into dollar-impact-per-minute."
      }
    }
  ],
